; RockCluster6 — 6th of 6 Rock terrain cluster variants (content-variety pass Task 6,
; 2026-08-26), the second MOSSY variant added alongside RockCluster5.tscn — see that
; scene's header for the full sourcing/attribution rationale (same pack, same 2
; Rock_Moss_N.fbx source files reused here, plus deliberately DIFFERENT arrangement/piece
; count so the two mossy clusters don't read as duplicates: 4 pieces here vs. 3 in
; RockCluster5, different scale/rotation/position per piece, different lead piece
; (Rock_Moss_5 first here vs. Rock_Moss_2 first in RockCluster5)).
;
; Source: 2x Rock_Moss_5.fbx + 2x Rock_Moss_2.fbx (Ultimate Nature Pack by Quaternius,
; CC0 1.0 Universal — same License.txt re-check as RockCluster5.tscn). Attributed in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres (assets_used already
; extended by RockCluster5.tscn's own addition — no further entry needed, same 2
; filenames).
;
; SCALE (measured via the same one-off SceneTree AABB script as RockCluster5.tscn — see
; that scene's header for the raw measured numbers): both raw pieces reused at 4 more
; distinct per-instance scales for a different silhouette mix than RockCluster5:
;   - Rock_A (Moss_5): scale 0.416132 -> height 0.240.
;   - Rock_B (Moss_5): scale 0.260083 -> height 0.150.
;   - Rock_C (Moss_2): scale 0.274653 -> height 0.190.
;   - Rock_D (Moss_2): scale 0.187920 -> height 0.130.
; Max piece height 0.240, matching the existing 4 clusters' ~0.25 height cap (D-42,
; rock.tres's own header) — the SAME cap, not a new number, and consistent with
; RockCluster5.tscn's 0.220 max. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: same open question as every
; prior cluster variant — the exact per-piece scale/spacing is a first-pass judgment call.
;
; Slab uses the same mossier grey-green tint as RockCluster3.tscn/RockCluster5.tscn
; (Color(0.48, 0.52, 0.42, 1)), 1.0x0.2x1.0 (post the "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0"
; cross-tile seam fix every current-generation terrain slab already carries).
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (a direct MeshInstance3D, matching
; RockCluster3/4/5's convention) — required, not cosmetic: OcclusionFader
; (scripts/world/occlusion_fader.gd) only skips a node by that exact name.
[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]

